From 10ee8d967a2d4b5f2aca9afeafb15dcf9dc5ffd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:08:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/32] (b) v2, part b-3: unique caption targets counted per
 name

Follow-up to the unique target of a caption that does not step its
counter (review finding N3):

- \theH<counter> was redefined with \protected@edef of itself. If it
  was undefined (an old-style counter made with \newcount), \csname
  made it \relax and the \edef a self-referencing macro: "TeX capacity
  exceeded". Now \the<counter> is used if \theH<counter> is undefined,
  as hyperref does.
- The old \theH<counter> was expanded early, outside the context that
  hyperref sets up for names (\@alph etc.). Now the suffix is added to
  a copy of its meaning, so hyperref expands it as usual.
- <n> was one global count, so adding a continued float anywhere
  renamed all later targets. Now it is counted per name: the continued
  parts of figure 1 get figure.1*1, figure.1*2, ..., independently of
  other floats.

The documentation of the socket caption/step now says why
\NextLinkTarget is not used (the kernel plug of refstepcounter/target
does not honour it), and the documentation of \@captionstepfalse names
its two uses (continued float, counter already stepped by the code;
review finding N4) and how code that has stepped the counter itself
gets the usual name.

Tests: caption-interface-001 test 20 now expects figure.16*1 and
figure.16*2; new tests for the count per name (interleaved figure and
table) and for a counter without \theH. float-024: figure.3*1 instead
of figure.3*3.
